window.docContents[78].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.ACD19.Ratchet.LibsignalBound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___ACD19___Ratchet___LibsignalBound":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session/ACD19/Ratchet › LibsignalBound.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 451 of 653 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (29)def CryptoGames.CKA.MakesAtMostQueriesdef CryptoGames.PRFPRNG.MakesAtMostQueriesabbrev Fig8Advabbrev LCtabbrev FsAdvdef fsSlotCountdef macForgeryTermdef ratchetCostBudgetdef ratchetFsAdapterBudgetdef fsRatchetCostBudgetdef evalTwoStage1abbrev CostedFitsabbrev CostedOpsSizeHonestabbrev CostedSampSizeHonestdef GRedBoundeddef CostedMidFitsdef GTwoStageBoundeddef GRedCostByKinddef GRed2CostByKindstructure FsCostedRedsdef fsCostedBoundsdef pubToADCosteddef multiSlotAdvCosteddef multiSlotAdvAuthCosteddef chainPRGTermAuthCosteddef saltPRFTermAuthCosteddef wireOtccaTermAuthCostedstructure Fig8CostedRedsdef fig8CostedBounds\n\nAdversary types, cost budgets and costed reduction bundles for the libsignal session boundTrusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except saltPRFTerm, wireOtccaTerm, multiSlotAdv and pubToAD; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. Those four are checked by Lean. Refine.SimProg, chainPRGTerm, fsShortBound, fsCompBound, fig8ShortBound and their …With forms are in Computational/Proofs/SpecLemmas/Session/ACD19/Ratchet/LibsignalBound.lean, checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.This file defines the adversary types, the message-blanking map of ACD19 Lemma 18 (Alwen, Coretti, Dodis, ePrint 2018/1037), the per-slot advantage terms of the symmetric-ratchet FS-AEAD bound, the explicit syntactic step-cost budgets, and the ReductionDsl costed reduction bundles used by libsignal_session_sm_r1_proto.Every reduction in the session and E2E bounds is represented as a first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction or ReductionDsl.TwoStageCostedReduction over atomicSig ℓ Pt (AtomicOps.lean, TargetCodecs.lean), where every base sort carries an explicit 32-byte block measure sz and multi-step chain iterations, skipped-key scans, and protobuf wire codecs are accounted at primitive granularity. GRedBounded and GTwoStageBounded enforce single-execution step-cost budgets (ratchetCostBudget, fsRatchetCostBudget, ratchetFsAdapterBudget), program size, target query counts, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local state and output bounds, while GRedCostByKind and GRed2CostByKind refine step-cost and target-query accounting when game queries are split by kind (online vs. offline random-oracle queries).Under the bucket-partitioned authenticity, DeliverForge parity-bucket, and switch-back privacy reductions, the 8-byte MAC-forgery part of the per-session bound scales as O(qep · q · macForgeryProb): 4 * macForgeryTerm C q = 4 * q * macForgeryProb is charged once per chain or bucket across privacy (qep + 2 challenge-epoch triples via redFSPriv and 2 * redFSPrivCoin), authenticity (qep + 1 last-leak tL buckets, split into honest-header and forged-header modes for 8 * macForgeryTerm C q per bucket), and DeliverForge (2 * qep + 1 shifted boundary cells plus ≤ 2 * max 1 qep unshifted (tL, par) buckets), with macForgeryProb ≥ 2⁻⁶⁴ for an 8-byte MAC tag. Compared with the earlier per-(t, tL, j) cell bound, this bucket-partitioned bound is formally incomparable: it drops the MAC-forgery term from O(qep² · q² · macForgeryProb) to O(qep · q · macForgeryProb) in exchange for up to 1.95× more PRF-PRNG terms, up to 1.74× more FS-AEAD terms (for q ≥ 1; 2.33× at q = 0, qep = 1), and a re-indexed, enlarged reduction family under ratchetCostBudget q (qep + 1) (see DEV-LS31 and DEV-C14 in Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md).\n\n\n\ndef CryptoGames.CKA.MakesAtMostQueriesL61–64 ↗#A makes at most q queries to the Fig. 3 CKA oracles (its own coins are unrestricted).\n\ndef CryptoGames.PRFPRNG.MakesAtMostQueriesL66–69 ↗#A makes at most q queries to the PRF-PRNG oracles (its own coins are unrestricted).\n\n\n\nabbrev Fig8AdvL80–82 ↗#Adversary against the Fig. 8 instance lFig8 (messages LibsignalMsgPublicPart × Plain ℓ).\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 84–96): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoGames.LibsignalSM.LibAdv, CryptoGames.LibsignalSM.lBlank\n\n\n\nabbrev LCtL113–114 ↗#Per-message AEAD ciphertext pairing wire (ser, tag) with the 32-byte SPQR salt.\n\nabbrev FsAdvL116–117 ↗#\n\ndef fsSlotCountL119–122 ↗#Active hybrid slot count 2 * qR + (maxForwardJumps + 1) of ACD19 Theorem 5 for a qR-query FS-AEAD adversary: at most qR main-chain slots and qR + maxForwardJumps + 1 lookahead-chain slots bounded by the skip window (DEV-LS10).\n\n4 declarations not shown (lines 124–154): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.pubToAD, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.multiSlotAdv, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.saltPRFTerm, CryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.wireOtccaTerm\n\ndef macForgeryTermL156–158 ↗#Per-chain MAC-forgery term qd * macForgeryProb C.F over at most qd decryptions (DEV-LS23), charged twice per chain (4 * macForgeryTerm C qd per FS-AEAD instance).\n\n\n\nCosted reduction bundles and budgets\n\ndef ratchetCostBudgetL164–166 ↗#Quadratic syntactic step-cost budget across session-layer reductions (maxForwardJumps = 25000).\n\ndef ratchetFsAdapterBudgetL168–171 ↗#Step-cost budget for the five single-slot and adapter reductions in FsCostedReds that perform no maxForwardJumps-step chain iterations.\n\ndef fsRatchetCostBudgetL173–177 ↗#Step-cost budget for the four two-stage FS-AEAD hybrid reductions (prgRedZero, multiRed, prgRedAuth, multiRedAuth).\n\ndef evalTwoStage1L179–189 ↗#Sequential evaluation of both stages of a unit-challenge TwoStageCostedReduction at query fuel fuel and default output dflt.\n\nabbrev CostedFitsL191–193 ↗#Recursive block, bit, and list size bound on a ReductionDsl value (ReductionDsl.ValFits).\n\nabbrev CostedOpsSizeHonestL195–198 ↗#Operator size-honesty obligation: each operator o increases the size bound by at most O.cost o.\n\nabbrev CostedSampSizeHonestL200–203 ↗#Sampler size-honesty obligation: each sampler s outputs values bounded by X.sCost s.\n\ndef GRedBoundedL205–231 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, target-query, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local output/state block-size bounds for a 1-stage CostedReduction at source query bound q, target query bound qOut, and step-cost budget costBudget. Size bounds are quantified per run via supportWhen (I.AnswerFits B) so interfaces with unbounded Bytes or .nat fields remain satisfiable.\n\ndef CostedMidFitsL233–238 ↗#Block-size bound on a two-stage mid-state.\n\ndef GTwoStageBoundedL240–267 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, target-query, operator/sampler size-honesty, and run-local mid-state and output block-size bounds for a TwoStageCostedReduction at fuel q, target query bound qOut, and step-cost budget costBudget.\n\ndef GRedCostByKindL269–282 ↗#Per-kind step-cost and target-query bound for a 1-stage CostedReduction whose game queries are partitioned by kind : κ → Fin n with per-kind budgets qKind: each query pays only its own kind's handler cost (CostBoundedByKind), and total target queries over (List.ofFn qKind).sum source queries are at most qOut. Paired alongside GRedBounded for size-honesty and run-local value-size bounds.\n\ndef GRed2CostByKindL284–297 ↗#Per-kind step-cost and target-query bound for a TwoStageCostedReduction under query partition kind and budgets qKind, requiring CostBoundedByKind across both stages, zero pre-challenge target queries (init, handlePre, chDone), and at most qOut total target queries. Paired alongside GRed2Bounded for size-honesty and run-local value-size bounds.\n\nstructure FsCostedRedsL299–391 ↗#Costed reduction programs for ACD19 Theorem 5 (pubRed, two-stage prgRedZero / multiRed, and direct-output prgRedAuth / multiRedAuth) and the per-message AEAD salt and wire hops on libsignal's symmetric ratchet (fsShortBound).\n\ndef fsCostedBoundsL393–417 ↗#Cost, program-size, query-count, and run-local size bounds for an FsCostedReds bundle at ratchet query bound qR and epoch cap qep: ratchetFsAdapterBudget qR qep on the five lightweight adapter/single-slot reductions and fsRatchetCostBudget qR qep on the four two-stage hybrid reductions (prgRedZero, multiRed, prgRedAuth, multiRedAuth).\n\ndef pubToADCostedL419–423 ↗#\n\ndef multiSlotAdvCostedL425–429 ↗#\n\ndef multiSlotAdvAuthCostedL431–437 ↗#multiSlotAdv evaluated via R.multiRedAuth and R.pubRed at query fuel qR (direct-output authenticity form).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 439–445): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.chainPRGTermCosted\n\ndef chainPRGTermAuthCostedL447–454 ↗#Slot j chain-PRG advantage evaluated via R.prgRedAuth and R.pubRed at query fuel qR (direct-output authenticity form).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 456–464): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.saltPRFTermCosted\n\ndef saltPRFTermAuthCostedL466–475 ↗#Slot j salt-PRF advantage evaluated via R.multiRedAuth on an FsCostedReds bundle (direct-output authenticity form).\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 477–485): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.LibsignalSession.wireOtccaTermCosted\n\ndef wireOtccaTermAuthCostedL487–496 ↗#Slot j wire-AEAD OT-CCA advantage evaluated via R.multiRedAuth on an FsCostedReds bundle (direct-output authenticity form).\n\nstructure Fig8CostedRedsL498–589 ↗#Costed reduction programs for ACD19 Theorem 1 (challSim), Lemma 18 (privRedB), bucket-partitioned Theorem 8 (redCKAAuth, redPRNGAuth, redFSAuth), and switch-back Theorem 12 (redCKAPriv, redCKAPrivU, redPRNGPriv, redFSPriv, redFSPrivCoin) on the Fig. 8 SM instance (fig8MixShortAuthV1, fig8MixShortPrivV1).\n\ndef fig8CostedBoundsL591–649 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, query-count, run-local size-honesty, and semantic target-query bounds for a Fig8CostedReds bundle R at SM query bound q and epoch cap qep.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/ACD19/Ratchet/LibsignalBound.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.ACD19.Ratchet.LibsignalBound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___ACD19___Ratchet___LibsignalBound"}});